WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.960
Henry Cavill's good looks and strong voice
make him a natural fit to play Superman, but

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.541
getting into godlike shape to play the Last
Son of Krypton is a superhuman feat in and

00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:10.200
of itself.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.740
How exactly did Cavill make himself faster
than a speeding bullet and more powerful than

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:15.580
a locomotive?

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.660
Let's find out.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.380
Exclusive gym

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.440
In order to turn himself into the Man of Steel,
Henry Cavill turned to the exclusive Gym Jones

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.970
— an invite-only gym known for training
athletes, military personnel — and the cast

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:28.840
of 300.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.420
Gym Jones is not your warm and cozy neighborhood
pilates studio.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.580
The gym prides itself on having no televisions,
no machines, no mirrors, and no comfortable

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.780
places to sit.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.240
And apparently, their walls have seen a fair
share of breakdowns — both physical and

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:43.920
psychological.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.400
Pushing limits

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.700
Cavill's training regimen essentially pushed
him into the realm of the superhuman.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:50.560
He explained,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.140
"I'm training two-and-a-half hours a day,
pushing my body beyond its normal limits."

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.080
"It's not just a physical thing, it's a psychological
thing as well."

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.950
Cavill recalled to ShortList one particularly
excruciating moment with his trainer Mark

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.980
Twight, during which, Cavill said he was...

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:09.560
"...Doing some horrible rowing sprint thing,
and I said, 'I can't do this Mark, I can't,

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.609
I'm done,' and he said, 'No you're not, don't
listen to the lies.'

00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:16.240
I kept on pulling and pulling until suddenly
I realized I had finished."

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.280
Strong foundation

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.420
Getting big is one thing.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.789
Staying Superman-sized, however, is an entirely
different story.

00:01:23.789 --> 00:01:27.620
"Yeah, well, ya know, gotta up the game every
year."

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.400
Henry Cavill's twice-daily training sessions
may have helped him get jacked, but once filming

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.940
actually started, that regimen went out the
window.

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:39.740
Still, the Man of Steel was able to minimize
the detrimental effects of a reduced workout

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.860
regimen, thanks to the ultra-solid muscle
base he'd built.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:43.680
Twight explained,

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.020
"Stable fitness requires a wide, solid foundation.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:50.969
The deeper that foundation, the more stable
that condition will be, and the easier it

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:51.900
is to maintain."

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.780
Catching Z's

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:59.120
Before Cavill even started training, Twight
laid down one extremely important stipulation

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:03.960
— the actor needed to get nine to ten hours
of sleep every single night for five months.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.520
Twight explained to Muscle &amp; Fitness,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.759
"If you don't get the sleep, if you can't
recover, then we can't continue with this

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.010
training and we won't achieve the objective."

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:17.900
"The HGH and testosterone secretion that happens
during these deep-sleep cycles is super-important."

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.600
The tailpipe

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.940
Cavill's trainer highly recommends ending
any Superman workout with something he likes

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:28.230
to call "the tailpipe," which was given its
name because, as Twight says, quote, "when

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.300
you're done, it feels like you've been sucking
on the tailpipe of a car."

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:37.400
Basically, you row 250 meters at full speed,
then hold two 24 kilogram kettlebells in the

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.520
rack position, and repeat three times.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.430
After that, your lungs will certainly feel
the burn — but you'll be able to get more

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:47.580
out of each subsequent workout, thanks to
the increased lung capacity and stamina.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.400
Can't skip cardio

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:53.960
Many people looking to bulk up don't get in
enough cardio, which does a lot more than

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.220
just make you faster than a speeding bullet.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.640
Cavill's strength coach Michael Blevins explained
to Men's Fitness,

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.280
"There's a misconception that cardio will
negatively impact muscle.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.680
A larger work capacity can allow you to train
harder and longer.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:10.950
Building muscle without conditioning is akin
to having an impressive engine without a gas

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.680
tank — it's worthless."

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.620
Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:19.240
One of Cavill's favorite ways to stay in shape
is by practicing Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.190
However, the actor doesn't just dabble in
the martial art.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.440
He trains with the best.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.460
Cavill frequently takes lessons from 10-time
Jiu-Jitsu world champion Roger Gracie.

00:03:28.469 --> 00:03:30.310
In an Instagram post, he wrote,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.770
"My B.J.J. has slipped by the wayside a bit
with my focus being on work but it's now time

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.740
to get back into it!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.520
Such an enjoyable way to train."

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.100
Chow down

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:45.359
While training to become Superman, Cavill
would generally eat between 3,500 and 5,000

00:03:45.359 --> 00:03:48.060
calories per day, including regular post-workout
shakes.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.060
He explained,

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.920
"You've got to eat protein first, then a little
bit of carbs.You've gotta keep your hunger

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:53.680
levels going."

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.820
"Unfortunately, Guinness is what I crave.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.360
It's not ideal for six pack abs."

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:02.120
Getting 5,000 calories meant roughly six meals
per day.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:08.280
HenryCavill.org lists samples of the 3,500
and 5,000 calorie meal plans on their "Man

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.140
of Steel Workout and Diet" page.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.040
Strength of character

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.800
Anyone can hire some skilled personal trainers
and put down a bunch of calories to get ripped,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.280
but playing Superman requires more than simply
lifting heavy objects and exhibiting lightning

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:21.820
speed.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.640
Being Superman requires inner strength.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.380
Twight told Muscle &amp; Fitness,

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.100
"Genuine accomplishment looks and feels different.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.020
It cannot be faked.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.540
By doing physically difficult things, by changing
his body of his own will, Henry changed his

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.100
attitude and his bearing.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.220
He looked huge.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:36.900
He walked huge.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.760
His attitude broadcast his physical capability."

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.460
Thanks for watching!

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.820
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

